{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>You shall not slaughter upon leaven, etc.</b> You shall not slaughter the Paschal offering on the fourteenth of Nisan until the leaven has been removed (Mekhilta)." "<b>And the fat of My feast shall not remain overnight.</b> Outside the altar." "<b>Until morning.</b> One might think disqualification by overnighting applies even to the arrangement [on the altar] — Scripture states: ״עַל מוֹקְדָה עַל הַמִּזְבֵּחַ כָּל הַלַּיְלָה״ (Leviticus 6)." "<b>And it shall not remain overnight.</b> 'Overnighting' means only at the column of dawn, as it says עַד בֹּקֶר — but all night long one may bring it up from the floor to the altar (Megillah 20)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:10.441630386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}